{"filename":"RFI-Technical-Outline-W52P1J-26-R-0147.pdf","uploadStatus":"Completed","dataProfile":{"date":"2026-06-12","type":"RFI","summary":"Request for Information issued by U.S. Army PEO EIS seeking industry input on capabilities, acquisition approaches, and pricing for Enterprise Data Analytics and AI Modernization Services to consolidate legacy analytics contracts. The RFI covers five capability areas including data mesh, AI/ML development, RAG implementation, legacy migration, and workforce training, with responses due July 24, 2026."},"text":"RFI No. W52P1J-26-R-0147 — UNCLASSIFIED — For Market Research Purposes Only — Page 1\nREQUEST FOR INFORMATION (RFI)\nEnterprise Data Analytics and AI Modernization\nServices\nRFI Number: W52P1J-26-R-0147\nIssued by: U.S. Army Program Executive Office, Enterprise Information Systems (PEO EIS)\nContracting Office: Army Contracting Command — Rock Island (ACC-RI)\nIssue Date: June 12, 2026 | Responses Due: July 24, 2026, 2:00 PM CT\nPrimary NAICS: 541512 — Computer Systems Design Services\nTHIS IS A REQUEST FOR INFORMATION ONLY. This RFI is issued solely for market\nresearch and planning purposes and does not constitute a solicitation. The Government will\nnot pay for any information or administrative costs incurred in response to this RFI.\n\nRFI No. W52P1J-26-R-0147 — UNCLASSIFIED — For Market Research Purposes Only — Page 2\n1. Purpose and Background\nPEO EIS is conducting market research to identify industry capabilities, recommended acquisition\napproaches, and rough order of magnitude (ROM) pricing for Enterprise Data Analytics and AI\nModernization Services. The anticipated effort would consolidate multiple legacy analytics contracts\nexpiring in FY2027 into a unified capability supporting Headquarters, Department of the Army and\nsubordinate commands.\nThe current environment includes approximately 340 on-premises Oracle databases, 280 SAS\nanalytics workloads, and 26 disparate business intelligence tools across 12 data centers. Prior\nmodernization efforts fielded point solutions without a common data or AI platform layer, resulting in\nduplicated ingestion pipelines and inconsistent security postures. The Government estimates the target\nuser population at 45,000 across unclassified (IL4/IL5) and classified (IL6) enclaves.\n2. Technical Capability Outline\nThe Government envisions five capability areas. Respondents should address their experience and\nrecommended approach for each area referenced in the draft Performance Work Statement (PWS)\ndated May 28, 2026.\nAreaCapabilityDescription\nCA-1Enterprise Data Mesh &\nGovernance\nFederated data products with centralized policy; catalog, lineage, and\nquality services; attribute-based access control (ABAC) aligned to Army\nICAM.\nCA-2AI/ML Development &\nMLOps\nModel development, registry, CI/CD for models, drift monitoring, and\ncompliance with DoDD 3000.09 and the NIST AI Risk Management\nFramework.\nCA-3Retrieval-Augmented\nGeneration (RAG)\nGrounded question answering over unclassified and classified corpora with\ncitation, access-aware retrieval, and measurable answer accuracy.\nCA-4Legacy Analytics MigrationMigration of Oracle and SAS workloads to a cloud lakehouse;\ndecommissioning plan; cost and performance baselining.\nCA-5Workforce EnablementAI literacy training, role-based upskilling, and embedded data coaching for\nGovernment analysts.\n2.1 Technical Objectives\n•\nAchieve Initial Operating Capability (IOC) not later than 12 months after award; respondents should\nstate whether a shorter timeline is achievable and under what conditions.\n•\nSupport deployment to AWS GovCloud and/or Azure Government at Impact Level 5, with a path to\nIL6 for selected workloads.\n•\nDemonstrate RAG answer faithfulness of at least 90% on a Government-furnished evaluation set\nprior to production release.\n•\nReduce legacy analytics operating costs by at least 35% within 24 months of FOC.\n\nRFI No. W52P1J-26-R-0147 — UNCLASSIFIED — For Market Research Purposes Only — Page 3\n•\nProvide the Government unlimited rights in all mission-specific models, prompts, and configurations\ndeveloped under the contract.\n2.2 Constraints and Interfaces\n•\nIntegration with Army ICAM for identity and ABAC attribute propagation is mandatory; Government\nwill furnish integration endpoints.\n•\nSolutions must interoperate with GCSS-Army, LMP, Advana, and Army Vantage data sources.\n•\nAll AI-generated outputs presented to end users must carry source citations and a confidence\nindication.\n•\nContinuous ATO (cATO) practices are preferred; respondents should describe their control\ninheritance approach and typical time-to-ATO.\n3. Questions for Industry\nRespondents are requested to answer the following. Responses to Section 3 shall not exceed 10\npages.\n#Question\nQ1What contract type (or mix of types) do you recommend for this effort and why?\nQ2Should the Government pursue a single award or a multiple award IDIQ? Explain the trade-offs.\nQ3What is a realistic timeline to IOC, and what Government-furnished items drive the critical path?\nQ4Describe your experience delivering RAG capabilities in DoD environments, including corpus size, user\ncounts, and measured accuracy.\nQ5What is your recommended approach to evaluating and continuously monitoring generative AI output\nquality?\nQ6Provide ROM pricing: fully burdened labor rates for key categories and estimated annual cloud/ODC costs.\n4. Submission Instructions\n•\nResponses are due no later than 2:00 PM Central Time on July 24, 2026, via email to\nusarmy.ria.acc.mbx.eis-analytics-rfi@army.mil.\n•\nFormat: PDF or Microsoft Word; 12-point font minimum for narrative; 25-page limit excluding cover\npage and capability matrices.\n•\nInclude company name, CAGE code, UEI, socioeconomic status, and applicable contract vehicles\non the cover page.\n•\nMark any proprietary information; unmarked responses will be treated as releasable for\nGovernment planning purposes.\n\nRFI No. W52P1J-26-R-0147 — UNCLASSIFIED — For Market Research Purposes Only — Page 4\n•\nQuestions regarding this RFI must be submitted in writing by July 2, 2026. Answers will be posted\nvia amendment on SAM.gov.\n5. Anticipated Schedule of Events\nEventDate\nRFI issuedJune 12, 2026\nIndustry questions dueJuly 2, 2026\nGovernment answers posted (Amendment 0001)July 10, 2026\nRFI responses dueJuly 24, 2026\nVirtual Industry Day (tentative)August 18, 2026\nDraft solicitation release (projected)1st Quarter FY2027\n6. Government Points of Contact\nContract Specialist: Ms. Dana Whitfield, ACC-RI — dana.k.whitfield.civ@army.mil — (309) 555-0166\nContracting Officer: Mr. Gerald Osei, ACC-RI — gerald.a.osei.civ@army.mil — (309) 555-0142\nTelephone inquiries will not be accepted. All communications regarding this RFI shall be directed to the\nContract Specialist in writing.","embeddings":[{"content":"Document name: RFI-Technical-Outline-W52P1J-26-R-0147.pdf \n\nRFI No. W52P1J-26-R-0147 — UNCLASSIFIED — For Market Research Purposes Only — Page 1 REQUEST FOR INFORMATION (RFI) Enterprise Data Analytics and AI Modernization Services RFI Number: W52P1J-26-R-0147 Issued by: U.S. Army Program Executive Office, Enterprise Information Systems (PEO EIS) Contracting Office: Army Contracting Command — Rock Island (ACC-RI) Issue Date: June 12, 2026 | Responses Due: July 24, 2026, 2:00 PM CT Primary NAICS: 541512 — Computer Systems Design Services THIS IS A REQUEST FOR INFORMATION ONLY. This RFI is issued solely for market research and planning purposes and does not constitute a solicitation. The Government will not pay for any information or administrative costs incurred in response to this RFI. RFI No. W52P1J-26-R-0147 — UNCLASSIFIED — For Market Research Purposes Only — Page 2 1. Purpose and Background PEO EIS is conducting market research to identify industry capabilities, recommended acquisition approaches, and rough order of magnitude (ROM) pricing for Enterprise Data Analytics and AI Modernization Services. The anticipated effort would consolidate multiple legacy analytics contracts expiring in FY2027 into a unified capability supporting Headquarters, Department of the Army and subordinate commands. The current environment includes approximately 340 on-premises Oracle databases, 280 SAS analytics workloads, and 26 disparate business intelligence tools across 12 data centers. Prior modernization efforts fielded point solutions without a common data or AI platform layer, resulting in duplicated ingestion pipelines and inconsistent security postures. The Government estimates the target user population at 45,000 across unclassified (IL4/IL5) and classified (IL6) enclaves. 2. Technical Capability Outline The Government envisions five capability areas. Respondents should address their experience and recommended approach for each area referenced in the draft Performance Work Statement (PWS) dated May 28, 2026. AreaCapabilityDescription CA-1Enterprise Data Mesh & Governance Federated data products with centralized policy; catalog, lineage, and quality services; attribute-based access control (ABAC) aligned to Army ICAM. CA-2AI/ML Development & MLOps Model development, registry, CI/CD for models, drift monitoring, and compliance with DoDD 3000.09 and the NIST AI Risk Management Framework. CA-3Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) Grounded question answering over unclassified and classified corpora with citation, access-aware retrieval, and measurable answer accuracy. CA-4Legacy Analytics MigrationMigration of Oracle and SAS workloads to a cloud lakehouse; decommissioning plan; cost and performance baselining. CA-5Workforce EnablementAI literacy training, role-based upskilling, and embedded data coaching for Government analysts. 2.1 Technical Objectives • Achieve Initial Operating Capability (IOC) not later than 12 months after award; respondents should state whether a shorter timeline is achievable and under what conditions. • Support deployment to AWS GovCloud and/or Azure Government at Impact Level 5, with a path to IL6 for selected workloads. • Demonstrate RAG answer faithfulness of at least 90% on a Government-furnished evaluation set prior to production release. • Reduce legacy analytics operating costs by at least 35% within 24 months of FOC. RFI No. W52P1J-26-R-0147 — UNCLASSIFIED — For Market Research Purposes Only — Page 3 • Provide the Government unlimited rights in all mission-specific models, prompts, and configurations developed under the contract. 2.2 Constraints and Interfaces • Integration with Army ICAM for identity and ABAC attribute propagation is mandatory; Government will furnish integration endpoints. •","contentNum":0,"startPosition":0,"endPosition":3719,"vector":"[-0.22407277,-0.075957246,-0.1631226,-0.4453925,0.27884358,0.05283549,0.09695285,0.0003426631,-0.2775204,-0.17294599,0.01661877,0.06859268,-0.016554344,0.16677554,0.16831315,0.06782443,0.16805096,0.5723256,-0.3703805,-0.009099029,-0.3936469,0.27214873,-0.052684933,-0.0807486,0.24079874,-0.04503742,0.054149777,-0.1703846,-0.2936898,-0.037256584,-1.4311006,-0.20560084,0.04291542,-0.2111786,0.06372987,0.10207144,-0.14909631,0.14503036,0.67964745,0.05897024,0.24421228,-0.016869865,-0.13892518,-0.27995455,0.0941444,-0.3823703,0.36805406,0.062330015,-0.48090202,0.2429674,0.31780276,-0.08328445,-0.33912826,0.07017474,-0.08138631,-0.17461914,-0.2865561,0.11469109,-0.1860657,-0.030250106,0.17061068,0.4295764,0.18743779,0.48487717,-0.17114535,-0.080152005,-0.009532178,0.20664017,0.32338327,-0.27716154,-0.101805806,-0.10995827,0.3897673,0.39519784,0.011775412,0.018130291,-0.2710044,-0.16621338,-0.09184798,-0.45808,-0.028745823,-0.018951867,-0.13585606,0.17623009,0.29492188,0.31781164,0.2366253,0.10000627,0.00013096801,0.02000453,-0.2602478,0.017726997,-0.46102637,-0.0992894,0.038360834,0.13123932,0.075463064,-0.1326964,-0.12956396,-0.05510079,-0.27103662,-0.08453043,0.34600532,-0.07929681,0.0546975,0.13491893,0.67862093,0.014999509,-0.117