ize, user counts, and measured accuracy. Q5What is your recommended approach to evaluating and continuously monitoring generative AI output quality? Q6Provide ROM pricing: fully burdened labor rates for key categories and estimated annual cloud/ODC costs. 4. Submission Instructions • Responses are due no later than 2:00 PM Central Time on July 24, 2026, via email to usarmy.ria.acc.mbx.eis-analytics-rfi@army.mil. • Format: PDF or Microsoft Word; 12-point font minimum for narrative; 25-page limit excluding cover page and capability matrices. • Include company name, CAGE code, UEI, socioeconomic status, and applicable contract vehicles on the cover page. • Mark any proprietary information; unmarked responses will be treated as releasable for Government planning purposes. RFI No. W52P1J-26-R-0147 — UNCLASSIFIED — For Market Research Purposes Only — Page 4 • Questions regarding this RFI must be submitted in writing by July 2, 2026. Answers will be posted via amendment on SAM.gov. 5. Anticipated Schedule of Events EventDate RFI issuedJune 12, 2026 Industry questions dueJuly 2, 2026 Government answers posted (Amendment 0001)July 10, 2026 RFI responses dueJuly 24, 2026 Virtual Industry Day (tentative)August 18, 2026 Draft solicitation release (projected)1st Quarter FY2027 6. Government Points of Contact Contract Specialist: Ms. Dana Whitfield, ACC-RI — dana.k.whitfield.civ@army.mil — (309) 555-0166 Contracting Officer: Mr. Gerald Osei, ACC-RI — gerald.a.osei.civ@army.mil — (309) 555-0142 Telephone inquiries will not be accepted. All communications regarding this RFI shall be directed to the Contract Specialist in writing.","contentNum":1,"startPosition":3034,"endPosition":6201,"vector":"[-0.20411614,-0.056421995,-0.44469061,-0.42449373,0.17777324,-0.09435246,0.08353739,0.00037790174,-0.03325414,-0.23616779,0.1107111,0.07508964,0.04195332,0.14196596,0.23911694,-0.09058711,0.08443257,0.29347405,-0.2532552,-0.107062355,-0.45431048,0.22928813,0.00815017,-0.0074724033,0.38484335